      {
        "variation": "default",
        "version": "initial",
        "items": [],
        "primary": {
          "eyebrow": "The idea",
          "title": "An organ for every stage, not only for churches",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In 2013 Yves Rechsteiner became artistic director of Toulouse les Orgues. His idea: a pipe organ that could leave the church. “The aim was to have an instrument performing out of churches for any musical project with pipe organ.”",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "start": 126,
                  "end": 229,
                  "type": "em"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "In 2017 the project stopped for financial reasons. Two years later Rechsteiner saw a teaser of Stephan Eicher's show Die Automaten, built with Decap instruments, and met Tony Decap. Tony had experience with movable pipe organs and had already developed his own wind control. Rechsteiner ordered a MIDI-controlled instrument.",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "start": 117,
                  "end": 130,
                  "type": "em"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "image": {
            "dimensions": {
              "width": 710,
              "height": 542
            },
            "alt": "Dancers on stage in front of L'Explorateur, an organist at the console",
            "copyright": null,
            "url": "https://images.prismic.io/decap/E8ZDXmUAI2SXqix2_20221008_mohaibalazs_074-3-3.jpeg?auto=format,compress",
            "id": "E8ZDXmUAI2SXqix2",
            "edit": {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 0,
              "zoom": 1,
              "background": "transparent"
            }
          },
          "video": {
            "link_type": "Media"
          },
          "image_brief": "Dancers on stage in front of L'Explorateur, an organist at the console, 4:3",
          "media_side": "Image left",
